  "IKRigController_docs": {
    "get_controller": "X.get_controller(ik_rig_definition) -> IKRigController\r\nUse this to get the controller for the given IKRig\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    ik_rig_definition (IKRigDefinition): \r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    IKRigController:",
    "set_skeletal_mesh": "x.set_skeletal_mesh(skeletal_mesh) -> bool\r\nSets the preview mesh to use. Loads the hierarchy into the asset's IKRigSkeleton.\nReturns true if the mesh was able to be set. False if it was incompatible for any reason.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    skeletal_mesh (SkeletalMesh): \r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    bool:",
    "apply_auto_generated_retarget_definition": "x.apply_auto_generated_retarget_definition() -> bool\r\nAnalyse the skeleton to see if it matches a known template and automatically generates all retarget chains and sets the pelvis\nReturns true if a matching skeletal template was found and the retarget definition for it was applied.\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    bool:",
    "apply_auto_fbik": "x.apply_auto_fbik() -> bool\r\nAnalyse the skeleton to see if it matches a known template and automatically generates a full body IK setup\nReturns true if a matching skeletal template was found and the FBIK setup for it was applied.\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    bool:",
    "get_retarget_chains": "x.get_retarget_chains() -> Array[BoneChain]\r\nGet read-only access to the list of Chains.\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    Array[BoneChain]:",
    "get_retarget_root": "x.get_retarget_root() -> Name\r\nGet the name of the Pelvis Bone of the retargeting (can only be one).\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    Name:",
    "get_root_motion_bone": "x.get_root_motion_bone() -> Name\r\nGet the bone used to store root motion for the skeleton (could be different from the root of the hierarchy).\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    Name:"
  },
  "IKRetargeterController_docs": {
    "get_controller": "X.get_controller(retargeter_asset) -> IKRetargeterController\r\nGet the controller for the given retargeter asset\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    retargeter_asset (IKRetargeter): an IK Retarget asset\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    IKRetargeterController: the controller with an API for modifying the given retarget asset",
    "set_ik_rig": "x.set_ik_rig(source_or_target, ik_rig) -> None\r\nSet the IK Rig to use as the source or target (to copy animation FROM/TO)\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    source_or_target (RetargetSourceOrTarget): an enum specifying either \"Source\" or \"Target\"\r\n    ik_rig (IKRigDefinition):",
    "set_preview_mesh": "x.set_preview_mesh(source_or_target, preview_mesh) -> None\r\nSet the preview skeletal mesh for either source or target\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    source_or_target (RetargetSourceOrTarget): an enum specifying either \"Source\" or \"Target\"\r\n    preview_mesh (SkeletalMesh): a skeletal mesh asset to use as the preview mesh in the retarget editor (may be used on other meshes at runtime)",
    "auto_map_chains": "x.auto_map_chains(auto_map_type, force_remap, op_name=\"None\") -> None\r\nUse string comparision to find \"best\" Source chain to map to each Target chain or clear the mappings\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    auto_map_type (AutoMapChainType): an enum specifying the type of mapping to perform (ie, Exact, Fuzzy or Clear)\r\n    force_remap (bool): if false, will only remap those mappings that unset/None\r\n    op_name (Name): if specified, will auto-map only the chain mapping in the specified op, otherwise applies to all ops",
    "auto_align_all_bones": "x.auto_align_all_bones(source_or_target, method=RetargetAutoAlignMethod.CHAIN_TO_CHAIN) -> None\r\nAutomatically align all bones in mapped chains and store in the current retarget pose.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    source_or_target (RetargetSourceOrTarget): Specifies whether to align bones in the source or target skeleton\r\n    method (RetargetAutoAlignMethod): The method to use for automatic alignment (defaults to ChainToChain)",
    "add_default_ops": "x.add_default_ops() -> None\r\nAutomatically add basic retargeting operations\nAdds these ops in the following order: Pelvis Motion, FK Chains, IK Chains, IK Solve and Root Motion\nIf any of these ops are already present, they will not be re-added.",
    "get_source_chain": "x.get_source_chain(target_chain_name, op_name=\"None\") -> Name\r\nGet the name of the source chain mapped to a given target chain (the chain animation is copied FROM).\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    target_chain_name (Name): the name of the target retarget chain to get a mapping for\r\n    op_name (Name): if specified, will get the source chain for that op (otherwise gets the first chain mapping in the op stack)\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    Name: the name of the source chain mapped to the given target chain (or None if not mapped)",
    "set_source_chain": "x.set_source_chain(source_chain_name, target_chain_name, op_name=\"None\") -> bool\r\nAssign a source chain to the given target chain. Animation will be copied from the source to the target.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    source_chain_name (Name): the name of the source retarget chain to assign\r\n    target_chain_name (Name): the name of the target chain to map\r\n    op_name (Name): if specified, will set the source chain only for that op (otherwise applies to all ops with a chain mapping)\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    bool:",
    "get_retarget_poses": "x.get_retarget_poses(source_or_target) -> Map[Name, IKRetargetPose]\r\nGet access to array of retarget poses.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    source_or_target (RetargetSourceOrTarget): Specifies whether to retrieve poses from the source or target skeleton\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    Map[Name, IKRetargetPose]: A reference to the map of retarget pose names to their pose data",
    "get_rotation_offset_for_retarget_pose_bone": "x.get_rotation_offset_for_retarget_pose_bone(bone_name, source_or_target) -> Quat\r\nGet a delta rotation for a given bone in the current retarget pose.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    bone_name (Name): The name of the bone to retrieve the rotation offset for\r\n    source_or_target (RetargetSourceOrTarget): Specifies whether the bone belongs to the source or target skeleton\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    Quat: The quaternion representing the rotation offset for the specified bone"
  },
  "Skeleton_docs": {
    "get_reference_pose": "x.get_reference_pose() -> AnimPose\r\nPopulates an Anim Pose with the reference poses stored for the provided USkeleton\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    AnimPose: \r\n\r\n    out_pose (AnimPose): Anim pose to hold the reference pose"
  },
